@page "/login"
@using BlazorDLR.Shared.Components

@*
    Web sign-in page — statically rendered, form-posts to /api/v1/auth/web/login (§7.5).

    Deliberately not a WASM page: a cookie cannot be set from inside an already-running
    WASM client, and the failure mode is subtle — the sign-in appears to work and the
    next request is anonymous. §7.5 is explicit about this and about the shape of the
    endpoint that sets the cookie.

    Antiforgery is off on this endpoint (§7.5's scoped decision), so this form does not
    need to fetch a token first.
*@

<PageTitle>Sign in — Dumb Luck Rides</PageTitle>

<div class="page page-standalone page-narrow form-page">
    <h1>Sign in</h1>

    <form method="post" action="/api/v1/auth/web/login">
        <label>
            User name
            <input name="userName" autocomplete="username" required autofocus />
        </label>
        <label>
            Password
            <input name="password" type="password" autocomplete="current-password" required />
        </label>
        <button type="submit">Sign in</button>
    </form>

    <p class="form-note"><a href="/auth/forgot-password">Forgot password?</a></p>
    <p class="form-note">No account yet? <a href="/register">Register</a>.</p>

    <SourceOfferFooter />
</div>
